WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.000
-Guys, this is my new
holiday single.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.467
I just flipped it around.

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:05.534
[ Laughter ]

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:06.934
This is me and Dolly Parton,

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.434
"Almost Too Early
for Christmas."

00:00:08.434 --> 00:00:10.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.467
♪♪

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:16.467
I talked about it on the show
last night because I put it out

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.834
on TikTok, and it was taken down
for legal issues.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:24.434
Because they said they didn't
have the rights to air the song

00:00:24.434 --> 00:00:26.367
on TikTok from the owner.

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.901
I wrote and sang the song.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:30.601
I go, "This is impossible."

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.767
But anyways, I'm in a legal
battle with myself.

00:00:32.767 --> 00:00:35.234
I'm currently in litigation.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.267
I think I'm gonna win.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.834
50/50.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.734
But it's been straightened out.
It is now available.

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:44.834
You can find it wherever on
the TikTok that I put out there.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.701
Which is a very innocent TikTok

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:49.067
of just me saying
how excited I was.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:52.067
Because you know, everyone
kind of starts this debate,

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.801
and now it's getting
earlier and earlier,

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.534
but it used to be Thanksgiving.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.501
They have the debate.
They go, "Should we --

00:00:58.501 --> 00:00:59.934
can we listen to holiday music?

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.701
Can we listen --
Do we play Mariah Carey now?"

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.667
And I say, yes.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:08.033
If it's a good a song,
play it whenever you want.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:10.334
But anyway, so I thought it'd
be funny if I wrote a song

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:13.367
called "Almost Too Early
for Christmas"...

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.968
...and you put it out Halloween.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.200
And so I wrote this song,

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.868
and then I didn't know
what to do with it.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:28.067
And then Dolly asked me
to do a scene in her movie

00:01:28.067 --> 00:01:31.100
coming up, called
"Mountain Magic Christmas."

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:34.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.100
"I'll do anything.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.434
I'll do
whatever you want me to do.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.167
I'll do --
Dolly Parton, sure.

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:40.567
I'll come,
I'll be the camera operator.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.067
Whatever you want me to do,
I'm there.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.601
So I go to Tennessee,
which inspired me for my beard.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:48.434
And, yeah,
the question no one's asking.

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:50.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.634
So I go there, and she goes,
"What song do you want to do?

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:56.200
What song do you want to do?"
And she's so cool.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.367
It's Dolly Parton.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:00.501
And I will say,
I wish that I worked --

00:02:00.501 --> 00:02:03.334
I was there in the morning
to the afternoon.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:06.234
I wish it was 9:00 to 5:00,
but it was 10:00 to 3:00.

00:02:06.234 --> 00:02:07.501
[ Laughter ]
I know, I know.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.667
Hey, I can still dream.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:11.534
But she said,
"What song do you want to do?"

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:16.901
I go, "A song?
I'll do anything with you."

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:18.200
And so we're
going through songs.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.834
I couldn't believe
she wanted to sing something.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.667
I go, "I actually
just wrote this song,

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.200
'Almost Too Early
for Christmas,'

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.968
could fit in with this theme."

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:26.667
She goes, "I want to hear it."

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.434
I go,
"You want to hear this song?"

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.167
So I just couldn't believe
ever that she even wanted

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.501
to hear the song.

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.367
So I'm playing
it off my phone or something.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:37.334
I'm like, "That's it,"
and she goes, "I love it."

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:39.667
So next thing I know,
I sent the track to her,

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:44.300
and she records it, like, in a
night and sends it back to me

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.567
and harmonizes,
and it sounds awesome.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:49.200
Can we just play
one second of it?

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:56.801
-♪ It's almost too early
for Christmas ♪

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.367
-♪ Too soon
to be singing this song ♪

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:00.501
That's it!
Stop right there!

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.067
Stop right there!
No, stop right there!

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:04.234
We can't legally afford it!

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:07.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:10.601
We can't legally
play that music!

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:11.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.701 --> 00:03:13.300
It's too early!

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.100
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:18.834
Anyways, right now,
you can go on nothing

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.868
and listen to it 'cause...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:23.767
...legally, it's not out
till Friday morning, so...

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.300
But if you can find it
wherever I posted it,

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.601
you can listen to that.

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:30.601
And I want to thank you for that
and thank Dolly so much.

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.801
It's now almost out.

